            "review_text": "Arnewoodian\nNew Forest National Park Hampshire, United Kingdom58 contributions\n1\nElegant but pricey lakeside café\nApr 2019 • Solo\nAn elegant old-style (ie French patisserie influenced) café on the edge of Hoan Kiem Lake. Nice to sit and enjoy the view, but you pay for the privilege - a small black filter coffee is 53,000 Dong. A range of delicious looking pastries, but the first two I asked for were sold out. Settled for coconut cake with chocolate chips, which was very nice. A place to stop for a coffee and a treat, take a few pictures, and move on.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 25, 2019",
